      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8383",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The definition of $\\cosh{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\cosh{x} = \\dfrac{1}{2}(e^{x} + e^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u20612) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{2}^{-1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+{2}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{4+1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077555/example-8383.json",
          "file_sha256": "c42b926ca45100b1ec458ed589df8a6f28075f47f6809b86455b027df6a7a364"
