        {
          "question": "e-8738",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The definition of $\\sinh x$ is \n\n$$\n\\sinh{x} = \\dfrac{1}{2}(e^{x} - e^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}\u20611 & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{1}-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(e-\\frac{1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
